if we have array why collectio is come to picture..becoz array have some drawbacks like:

-arrays store only similar types of data
-collection store different type of data

-size of aaray is fixed
-size of collection is not fixed

-in array we can perfom Insert,Delete,Update,get
-predefined method of collection

| Array                                           | Collection                                                   |
| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Size of array is **fixed** after creation       | Size of collection is **dynamic (can grow or shrink)**       |
| Array can store **primitive types and objects** | Collection stores **only objects**                           |
| Array is part of **Java language**              | Collection is part of **Java Collections Framework**         |
| In array we use **index to access elements**    | In collection we use **methods like add(), remove(), get()** |
| Arrays have **limited built-in operations**     | Collections provide **many predefined methods**              |
| Arrays are **not flexible**                     | Collections are **more flexible and powerful**               |


